  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \n\nNorthwest flow aloft with surface high pressure of Canadian origin\nbuilding southeast into the Great Lakes and Ohio Valley today. This\nhigh will build across the region thru the end of the week. Dry \nconditions and below average temperatures can be expected with lows \nin the 50s and highs in the 70s to near 80. \n\nThe surface high shifts east this weekend which will allow for a\nwarming trend along with higher dew points. Shower and thunderstorms\nchances return along with increased heat and moisture. Upper level \nshortwave disturbances moving through the northwesterly flow aloft \ncould lead to periods of greater storm coverage at times.",
